Q: Capture KeyDown or KeyPress in .NET MAUI (Windows) A: <p>You can obtain the <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/uwp/api/windows.ui.xaml.uielement?view=winrt-22621" rel="nofollow noreferrer">UIElement</a> on which the key pressed events should be detected from <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/microsoft.maui.handlers.viewhandler.platformview?view=net-maui-7.0#microsoft-maui-handlers-viewhandler-platformview" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Handler.PlatformView</a>. And then hook up the native events.</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>var handler = mauiView.Handler;
UIElement? nativeView = handler?.PlatformView as UIElement;
if (nativeView != null)
{
    nativeView.KeyDown += this.PlatformView_KeyDown;
    nativeView.KeyUp += this.PlatformView_KeyUp;
    nativeView.PreviewKeyDown += this.PlatformView_PreviewKeyDown;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Here, <code>mauiView</code> is the view on which the key pressed events should be detected. Please note that this view should be focused for the key pressed events to be detected.</p>

